{"name":"Maiden Hair","hex":"#f5e9ca","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"maiden-hair","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of maidenhair."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/maiden-hair"}],"entries":[{"title":"Maidenhair (painting)","blocks":[{"text":"Maidenhair is a 1974 painting by the American artist Andrew Wyeth. It depicts a young bride-to-be sitting alone in the Old German Meeting House in Waldoboro, Maine."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c0/Andrew_Wyeth%27s_painting_Maidenhair%2C_1947%2C_tempera.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maidenhair_(painting)"},{"title":"Adiantum","blocks":[{"text":"Adiantum, the maidenhair fern, is a genus of about 250 species of ferns in the subfamily Vittarioideae of the family Pteridaceae, though some researchers place it in its own family, Adiantaceae. The genus name comes from Greek, meaning \"unwetted\", referring to the fronds' ability to shed water without becoming wet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Adiantum_pedatum_09905.JPG/330px-Adiantum_pedatum_09905.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adiantum"},{"title":"Virginity","blocks":[{"text":"Virginity is a social construct that denotes the state of a person who has never engaged in sexual intercourse. As it is not an objective term with an operational definition, social definitions of what constitutes virginity, or the lack thereof, vary. Heterosexual individuals may or may not consider loss of virginity to occur only through penile–vaginal penetration, while people of other sexual orientations often include oral sex, anal sex, or manual sex in their definitions of virginity loss. The term \"virgin\" encompasses a range of definitions, as found in traditional, modern, and ethical concepts. Religious rituals for regaining virginity exist in many cultures. Some men and women who practice celibacy after losing their virginity consider themselves born-again virgins."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-Youth_%281893%29.jpg/330px-William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-Youth_%281893%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virginity"},{"title":"Hair","blocks":[{"text":"Hair is a protein filament that grows from follicles found in the dermis. Hair is one of the distinguishing characteristics of mammals.\nThe human body, apart from areas of glabrous skin, is covered in follicles which produce thick terminal and fine vellus hair. Most common interest in hair is focused on hair growth, hair types, and hair care, but hair is also an important biomaterial primarily composed of protein, notably alpha-keratin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Gray945.png/330px-Gray945.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hair"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Old_German_Church%2C_Waldoboro%2C_ME.jpg/500px-Old_German_Church%2C_Waldoboro%2C_ME.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Old_German_Church%2C_Waldoboro%2C_ME.jpg/500px-Old_German_Church%2C_Waldoboro%2C_ME.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Old German Church and Cemetery","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOld_German_Church%2C_Waldoboro%2C_ME.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Adiantumhispidulum1web.jpg/120px-Adiantumhispidulum1web.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.